--TEST--
`Core\Env::mode` answers `Production` on a host that configured nothing, while the directive it reads is still unset — `rule:config/a-mode-is-five-defaults` and `rule:http-server/the-mode-ceiling-defaults-to-the-startup-mode` and spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The ceiling's row for a host that wrote no configuration at all is `production`, so a
// deployment is the restrictive one before an operator has said anything. This
// case ships no `nvs.toml`, which is exactly that host.
if (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env::Mode::Production) {
    echo "mode=Production", "\n";
} else {
    echo "mode=Development", "\n";
}

// `mode.default` is a directive like any other and nothing set it here, so
// `Core\Config::get` gives its built-in default — the same mode the member
// answers, read from the one table of defaults.
echo "directive=", Core\Config::get("mode.default") ?? "unset", "\n";

// Two cases, and a program can name either: the comparison above is a choice
// between them and not a test for the presence of one.
echo "development=", (Core\Env::mode() == Core\Env::Mode::Development) ? "true" : "false", "\n";
--EXPECT--
mode=Production
directive=production
development=false
